WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.762
Now we reverse the direction.

00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:09.552
The monthly sales table stores January, February, and March as separate columns.

00:00:09.552 --> 00:00:15.797
That is convenient for a fixed report, but less flexible for many analytical tasks.

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:21.137
Unpivoting turns those month columns back into row values.

00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:28.917
Long and wide are not labels for good and bad design; they are shapes suited to different tasks.

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:34.967
Long data is often easier for grouping, plotting, and scalable storage.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:41.797
Wide data is often convenient for human-readable reports or some modeling interfaces.

00:00:41.797 --> 00:00:44.917
Choose the shape required by the next step.
